WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.303
-It has now been
almost four months

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.939
since Hurricane Maria devastated
the island of Puerto Rico,

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.606
leaving millions
without electricity

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:09.008
and clean drinking water.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.043
Since then, the crisis
has all but completely

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:12.512
dropped out of the news cycle,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.214
so we thought we'd see how
recovery efforts are proceeding.

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.682
It's time for "The Check In."

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.484 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.186 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.521
Hurricane Maria was the worst

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.924
natural disaster on record
to hit Puerto Rico,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.993
a fact seemingly lost
on our president,

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.962
who almost immediately
gave himself a perfect score

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.531
on handling the crisis.

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:37.169
-I'd say it was a 10.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.438
I give ourselves a 10.

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:44.177
We have provided so much,
so fast, I would give a 10.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:47.346
-I bet young Donald Trump
wasn't one of those kids

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:48.815
you let grade his own homework.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.215
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:52.585
"What would you give yourself
on your volcano project?"

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.353
"An A-plus.
It's a great volcano.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.721
Very lifelike."

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:56.923
"Really?

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.157
Because all you did was dip

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.858
a roll of toilet paper
in kerosene

00:00:59.858 --> 00:01:01.694
and light it on fire."

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:05.197
Now, those 10 out of 10 comments
were made back in October.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:08.267
So what's that perfect score
look like since then?

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.702
-Many Puerto Ricans spent

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.538
their first Christmas since
Hurricane Maria without power.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:13.873
More than three months
after the storm,

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.274
the island's electrical grid

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:18.677
is operating
just 65% -- 65% -- of capacity.

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:21.714
The ongoing crisis there
is taking a terrible toll.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.349
-The challenges
that they're facing,

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.285
particularly
in the remote areas,

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.419
rural areas, smaller towns,

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:29.388
are much the same now
as they were then.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:32.124
-What we're seeing is really
a lowering of the bar

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.693
of what kinds of basic services

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:36.796
are American citizens
entitled to?

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.766
You know, it's gonna be 100 days
without electricity

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:43.436
for more than half
of this U.S. territory.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.172
-If that's what Trump
considers a 10,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.040
what would a 9 be?

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.943
Accidentally sending
an outbreak monkey?

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.111
"Okay, I'll be honest.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.712
We sent a monkey
to help with the cleanup.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:54.947
It had a deadly virus.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.582
Long story short,
9 out of 10."

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.384
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.585
But don't worry, Puerto Rico.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.487
The president might not
be on the case,

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.721
but there's still Ben Carson.

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:03.890
He's a brain surgeon,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.658
took a Hippocratic oath,
and he's the Secretary

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.893
of Housing
and Urban Development.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.194
Surely, he had something
a little more helpful

00:02:09.194 --> 00:02:10.796
to say about this crisis.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.766
Here he is being asked how long
he thought HUD was going to be

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.000
in Puerto Rico.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.036
-Any idea how many years?

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:20.606
-Somewhere between 1 and 100.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:24.043
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.279
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.682
-Ben Carson might be the first
brain surgeon in history

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:33.552
to leave a sponge
inside his own head.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:36.021
"So as you can see
from your x-ray,

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:37.657
everything is fine.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.292
Mine, on the other hand..."

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.594
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.895
Now, to give you
a sense of the dysfunction

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.196
in the recovery efforts,

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:46.265
a contract for hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.769
was afforded to a small company
in Whitefish, Montana --

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.371
which also happens
to be the hometown

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.405
of interior secretary
Ryan Zinke --

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:55.174
to help restore
Puerto Rico's electrical grid.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.276
But almost immediately,

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.643
there was scrutiny
over the contract.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:03:00.646
First of all, the company
only had two employees

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.248
when Hurricane Maria hit.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.584
Two employees
to handle a Hurricane!

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.085
That's like trying
to solve Afghanistan

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.088
with the Mayberry
Police Department.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.190
Now, after much outcry
and overbilling issues,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.459
the Whitefish contract
has since been canceled,

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.928
but Puerto Rico is still
desperately in need of help.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:18.665
In November, for example,
the White House asked Congress

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.100
for $44 billion
in hurricane aid --

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.002
funds designated
for Texas and Florida.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.475
Even worse, Trump and the GOP
passed a tax plan

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.744
that disproportionately harms
Puerto Ricans

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.312
by treating
the American territory

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.814
as a foreign entity

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.016
and imposing unfair
and cruel taxes on them

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.284
which could result in the loss

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.119
of hundreds of thousands
of jobs there.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.421
-Congress has just passed
this tax bill

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:46.692
which had this really sinister
effect, if I may,

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:47.894
on Puerto Rico.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.463
-It has an insidious,
pernicious effect

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.865
on manufacturing in Puerto Rico.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.268
-It puts an excise tax,
an import tax,

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.403
on products and services
for Puerto Rico.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.938
-A tax that's not there now.
-That's not there now.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.873
-That would cripple
the Puerto Rican economy.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.809
-Well, it's crippled already.
It will obliterate it.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:08.113
This would be a much more
devastating blow to our economy

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:09.982
than Irma and Maria
put together.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:11.617
-The Republican tax bill
is worse

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.719
than two Hurricanes
put together.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.054
In fact,
that's how meteorologists

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.390 line:0%
are going to start
classifying them from now on.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.226 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:23.096
Perhaps the only thing Trump
has actually succeeded in doing

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.463
when it comes to Puerto Rico

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.699
is diverting attention
away from the crisis.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.534
Over the weekend,
the news cycle was dominated

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.902
by Trump's alleged remarks

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.204
that countries like Haiti
and African nations

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.506
are [bleep]holes,

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.941
which the governor
of Puerto Rico

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.776
also had to respond to.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:41.547
-I think it is
an S-H-I-T-T-Y comment.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.484
It is completely unacceptable.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:46.686
-I get it.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.987
He's spelling it

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.421
so that Trump wouldn't
understand what he's saying.

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:51.457
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.363
"Call the NSA.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.332
I need our very best
code breaker on this."

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:02.001
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.802
But Trump's comments
are indicative

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.171
of his lackluster response
to Hurricane Maria.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:07.607
From the very beginning,
he treated

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.909
the American citizens
of Puerto Rico much differently

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.343
than those in Florida and Texas.

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:13.346
And that's alarming,
considering Puerto Rico

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.280
was already facing
a brutal recession

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.782
before the hurricanes hit

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:19.552
that left 44% of the population
impoverished.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.953
And now, instead of actually

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.488
helping
the people of Puerto Rico,

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.989
Republicans and Trump
passed a law

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:25.291
that would exacerbate

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.326
the already dire
economic situation there.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.095
And that can only be described
as, really --

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.563
What's the word I'm looking for?

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.865
-S-H-I-T-T-Y.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.733
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's the one.

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:36.102
This has been "The Check In."

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.770 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.405 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

